    ".ARC",
    "Norton Backup Archive",
    "4.0",
    "An ARC file is a backup file created by Norton software products, such as Norton 360 and Norton Online Backup. It contains a backup of computer files created automatically by the software, which may include personal user files as well as system files. Since ARC files can include all personal and system files, they may be very large in size. ARC files are used for storing and recovering files in the event of accidental deletion or system failure. They may be backed up to an off-site location using Norton Online Backup. NOTE: Norton 360 no longer supports ARC files. Windows Symantec Norton Online Backup —  (Discontinued). Trial Mac Symantec Norton Online Backup —  (Discontinued). Trial. An ARC file is a compressed file archive created either as a Macintosh Hierarchical File System (HFS) archive or an MS-DOS archive using standard MS-DOS compression. It contains a collection of compressed files, each being compressed potentially with a different compression technique. ARC files were commonly used in the late 1980s and early 1990s. However, they are rarely used now and have been replaced by newer, more efficient compression algorithms. NOTE: While ARC files were used primarily for MS-DOS and older versions of Macintosh computers, several current programs can still open them, such as StuffIt and WinZip. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Corel WinZip. 7-Zip. PeaZip. FreeArc. ConeXware PowerArchiver. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. The Unarchiver. Linux FreeArcFree. Contains music, images, and other data used by Cabelas African Safari; named data.arc and is located in the /PSP_GAME/USRDIR/ directory on Sony PSP discs; Cabelas African Safari is available for Windows PC, Xbox, Playstation 2, and PSP. The DATA.ARC file is referenced by the African Safari game and should not be manually opened by the user. Windows Activision Cabelas African Safari. Archive file used by Nintendo games; contains game properties, such as images, textures, objects, UI layouts, and levels; typically stored within ROMs; can be edited to customize gameplay. Windows Reggie! Level Editor. SZS ModifierFree. Backup file created for mobile devices that use the Symbian open source operating system; contains both personal and system backup data from the mobile device; used for restoring data in the event it is lost. Example ARC files include backup.arc, Messages.arc, Calendars.arc, and Bookmarks.arc. Windows Nokia PC Suite. Nokisoft Noki. NbuExplorerFree. An ARC file is a compressed archive used by discontinued console versions of Minecraft, which are collectively referred to as Minecraft: Legacy Console Edition. It contains UI elements and textures, language files, and structure data. In the past, developer 4J Studios published console-specific versions of Minecraft. These versions of Minecraft were named for the console on which they could be played. For example, the PlayStation Vita version of Minecraft was named Minecraft for Playstation Vita. Players often refer to these versions of Minecraft, which have since been replaced by Minecraft Bedrock Edition, as Minecraft: Legacy Console Edition. All Minecraft: Legacy Console Edition games include ARC archives. While players are not meant to open or edit these files (or the game data they contain), Minecraft: Legacy Edition modders have created tools that allow them to extract assets from and add assets to ARC files. You can open and manage ARC files with ARC Studio (Windows) or MCCToolChest (Windows). Windows ARC Studio. MCCToolChestFree. An ARC file is a game data file used by WWE 2K18 and 2K19. It contains cached game data. The games ARC file is named Chunk0.arc. Both WWE 2K18 and 2K19 cache certain game data to speed up the games startup time. The games store this cached data in and load it from Chunk0.arc. Most WWE 2K18 and 2K19 players will never encounter or need to modify Chunk0.arc. However, modders who have installed 2K18 or 2K19 mods must delete or clear Chunk0.arc, to clear the games cache so their installed mods load correctly. Otherwise, the games will crash at startup. Chunk0.arc - The name assigned to WWE 2K18 and 2K19s ARC files. Chunk0.arc is not meant to be opened. Windows 2K Sports WWE 2K18. 2K Sports WWE 2K19.",
    "Windows Symantec Norton Online Backup —  (Discontinued). Trial. Mac Symantec Norton Online Backup —  (Discontinued). Trial. Windows Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe. Corel WinZip. 7-Zip. PeaZip. FreeArc. ConeXware PowerArchiver. Mac Smith Micro StuffIt Deluxe Mac 16. The Unarchiver. Linux FreeArc. Windows Activision Cabelas African Safari. Windows Reggie! Level Editor. SZS Modifier. Windows Nokia PC Suite. Nokisoft Noki. NbuExplorer. Windows ARC Studio. MCCToolChest. Windows 2K Sports WWE 2K18. 2K Sports WWE 2K19.",
