    ["backup_files",
    ".WIN",
    "FoxPro Window Settings",
    "3.4",
    "Contains FoxPro window definitions and statuses; used for backing up window settings; can be restored using the RESTORE WINDOW command. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Backup of a Windows system file; restores the original file if it is deleted or becomes corrupted; may be referenced by the Windows Restore program during the system restore process. Windows Used by the system as a data recovery file if needed. A WIN file is an asset package created by GameMaker Studio, a cross-platform game engine. It is distributed with a game developed by GameMaker Studio and contains all the assets for the game, which include code, scripts, sounds, sprites, fonts, shaders, and textures. The WIN file type is one of several asset package types that a game developer may choose from to accompany the distribution of his game. The package format is designed to protect assets from being modified by users looking to alter gameplay. Users playing games that utilize the WIN file type can find the WIN file in the same directory as the.EXE game file. Examples of games developed by GameMaker Studio that utilize the WIN file include Rivals of Aether, IMSCARED, Deltarune, and Undertale. WIN files are not meant to be opened by a user. They are meant to be referenced by the games for which they contain assets. However, users who enjoy modifying gameplay can open WIN files for the Undertale and Deltarune games (and possibly other GameMaker Studio games) with UndertaleModTool. NOTE: Users should not modify games that they are legally restricted from modifying. data.win - Default filename of a WIN file packaged with a game created by GameMaker Studio. Windows UndertaleModToolFree. A WIN file is a backup file created by Team Win TWRP, a third-party backup and recovery program for Android devices. It contains a copy of some or all of the files stored on a users Android phone (or other device). WIN files can be used only on the device that created them. Team Win TWRP is an unofficial custom recovery application for Android. It allows users to back up their Android devices entire file system, as well as subsets of that system. TWRP backups are saved as WIN files. To create a backup, users select the Backup button that appears in TWRPs main menu. Users can then export the WIN backup TWRP creates to an external hard drive, to keep the backup separate from their Android device. You can use a WIN file to restore the backed-up files or file system it contains. To do so, transfer your WIN file to the Android device that created it. Then, open Team Win TWRP and select the Restore button. From there, follow TWRPs prompts to restore your backed-up files. Android Team Win TWRPFree.",
    "Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro. Windows Used by the system as a data recovery file if needed. Windows UndertaleModTool. Android Team Win TWRP.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".WBX",
    "Winbox Address Book",
    "3.3",
    "A WBX file is a backup file used by Winbox, a utility that allows admins to manage their MikroTik routers. It contains the contents of a Winbox address book. WBX files are most commonly named addresses.wbx. Winbox is a GUI utility that those who own MikroTik routers can use to manage their routers (or routers) settings. To allow router admins to easily transfer routers MAC addresses, IP addresses, and login credentials between computers, Winbox gives users the option to export this data in WBX files. WBX files are most useful for those who use Winbox to manage multiple routers, allowing them to import a series of router addresses and login information at once, rather than entering that information manually on many computers. addresses.wbx - A file containing router address and login information saved using Winbox. You can use Winbox to import your WBX file and use it as your Winbox address book. To do so, open the program and select Tools → Import... Windows MikroTik WinboxFree.",
    "Windows MikroTik Winbox.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".GS-BCK",
    "Genius Scan Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "A GS-BCK file is a backup file created by The Grizzly Labs Genius Scan, an Android app used to scan and export documents. It contains backup data of one or more documents that have been scanned by Genius Scan. To create a GS-BCK file, select Settings in Genius Scan, choose Back up Genius Scan data, select a destination folder, and tap OK. To restore a GS-BCK file, select Settings in Genius Scan, choose Restore a previous back-up, and select the GS-BCK file you want to restore. After choosing the GS-BCK file, the Genius Scan app will restart and your documents will be available. backup_[year]-[month]-[day].gs-bck - The naming convention for GS-BCK files. An example of a GS-BCK file created on September 12, 2018 would be backup_2018-09-12.gs-bck. Android The Grizzly Labs Genius Scan.",
    "Android The Grizzly Labs Genius Scan.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".SCRIPA",
    "Scarlet IPA Backup",
    "3.3",
    "A SCRIPA file is an iOS app backup created by Scarlet, an App Store alternative for iOS devices. It contains an.IPA (iOS application) file and a users app data. Scarlet users can create SCRIPA files to back up their app settings or game progress alongside an apps IPA file. Scarlet is an unofficial, third-party alternative to the iOS App Store. In addition to allowing a user to download and install iOS applications, by sideloading their IPA files, Scarlet includes many advanced features. One of these features is the ability to back up apps and their related data in SCRIPA files. For example, if a user has modified an apps settings, they might want to back up that app as a SCRIPA file. Doing so creates a copy of the app that retains their settings data, which the user can quickly reinstall and resume using (with their settings already in place) if needed. How to back up an app as a SCRIPA file To create a SCRIPA file, a Scarlet user must: Open Scarlet and select Modify IPA. Navigate to and select the IPA file for which theyd like to create a SCRIPA file. Select Enable Backup/Restore. Go to their Home screen, long-press the app , and select Backup. Scarlet will then create a SCRIPA file that contains the apps IPA file and the users app data. You can use Scarlet (iOS) to restore the iOS app backup a SCRIPA file contains. To do so, open Scarlet, go to the Installed screen, and then browse to and open your SCRIPA file. iOS ScarletFree.",
    "iOS Scarlet.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".TBK",
    "FoxPro Memo Backup",
    "3.3",
    "Project file created by ToolBook, a program used by subject matter experts (SMEs) for creating e-learning materials; may save a series of screens with text labels, graphics, and embedded multimedia content; used for saving interactive quizzes, software simulations, and other learning modules. ToolBook TBK files can be delivered through several mediums, including HTML pages, CD-ROMS, mobile device applications, and self-running executables (.EXE files). Windows SumTotal Systems ToolBook. Microsoft Internet Explorer with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Mozilla Firefox with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Mac Mozilla Firefox with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Linux Mozilla Firefox with SumTotal Neuron plug-inFree. Backup of a FoxPro table memo; corresponding table backup file uses a.BAK extension. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro.",
    "Windows SumTotal Systems ToolBook. Microsoft Internet Explorer with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Mozilla Firefox with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Mac Mozilla Firefox with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Linux Mozilla Firefox with SumTotal Neuron plug-in. Windows Microsoft Visual FoxPro.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BM3",
    "Sony Ericsson Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "Mobile phone backup file created by Sony Ericsson PC Suite, a program used for syncing mobile data with the PC; saves contacts, messages, notes, and other data on the phone; can be used to restore the phones state. NOTE: BM3 files are actually.ZIP files. However, the files within the Zip container are encrypted and are not viewable. Windows Sony Ericsson PC SuiteFree.",
    "Windows Sony Ericsson PC Suite.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".MDBACKUP",
    "iPhone Data Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "iPhone or iPod touch backup file created by iTunes, a digital media player; contains backup data for the device, which may include notes, SMS messages, pictures, contacts, and other data; used by iTunes for restoring device states. The data in MDBACKUP files are stored in a proprietary format which is only meant to be used by iTunes. However, some information may include plain text data, which can be read with a text viewer. NOTE: MDBACKUP files have been replaced by.MDDATA and.MDINFO files in more recent firmware versions for the iPhone and iPod Touch. Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor Mac Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Echo One File Juicer. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "Windows Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Mac Apple iTunes —  (Discontinued). Echo One File Juicer. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".SN2",
    "Drive Snapshot Second Differential Backup",
    "3.3",
    "Second differential backup created by Drive Snapshot; created after the primary.SNA backup and the first.SN1 backup files have been saved; contains only files and folders that have been changed since the first differential backup; can be mounted like a physical disk when opened with the Drive Snapshot program. Windows Tom Ehlert Drive Snapshot.",
    "Windows Tom Ehlert Drive Snapshot.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".PBX5SCRIPT",
    "Personal Backup Script",
    "3.3",
    "File created by Personal Backup, a program used for creating backups on the Mac; defines what data will be backed up and can be run periodically on a schedule in Personal Backup; used for saving and loading backup jobs and can be opened to run the job. Mac Intego Mac Premium Bundle X9.",
    "Mac Intego Mac Premium Bundle X9.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".VBK",
    "Veeam Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "Backup file created by Veeam virtual machine (VM) backup and recovery software; contains a full recovery backup of the VM and is the largest of the files created for any backup; allows a full restore of the state of the machine when it was last backed up. VBK files differ from.VRB files, which contain incremental backup changes since the time of the full backup. NOTE: VBK files can be very large (many gigabytes in size). For this reason, they are often backed up to low-cost storage devices such as tape backups. Windows Veeam Backup & Replication. DRM protected eBook used by VitalSource Bookshelf, an eBook application used for reading purchased textbooks; may contain a digital textbook created by one of many different publishers; requires a VitalSource Bookshelf account as well as the software client to open. The VitalSource Bookshelf software also allows users to access digital copies of textbooks you own in print. Mac VitalSource Bookshelf. Windows VitalSource Bookshelf. iOS VitalSource Bookshelf. Android VitalSource BookshelfFree.",
    "Windows Veeam Backup & Replication. Mac VitalSource Bookshelf. Windows VitalSource Bookshelf. iOS VitalSource Bookshelf. Android VitalSource Bookshelf.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".TRN",
    "SQL Server Transaction Log Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "Backup file created by Microsoft SQL Server, a relational database management system (RDBMS) application; contains a transaction log backup, which saves a history of committed and uncommitted database changes since the last checkpoint. TRN files are used for database restores and may be used with other TRN files to chain roll back to any previous database state. TRN files are often backed up with a.BAK file, which is the backup of the database. Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019.",
    "Windows Microsoft SQL Server 2019.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BKC",
    "Backup4all Backup Catalog",
    "3.3",
    "Backup catalog file created by Backup4all; contains a list of files and folders backed up using the Backup4all backup utility; BKC files can be restored to the original location or another hard drive using the Restore Wizard. Windows Softland Backup4all.",
    "Windows Softland Backup4all.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".LBF",
    "LG Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "An LBF file is a backup file created by backup software that comes pre-installed on LG Android phones. It contains a copy of the applications, contacts, messages, calendar entries, media, and settings stored on a phone. Multiple LG backup apps, including LG Backup and LG Mobile Switch, create and use LBF files. LG phones that run the Android operating system typically come with a pre-installed proprietary backup app. These apps allow users to manually back up their phones data and save that data in an LBF file. If a user wants to transfer their data to another LG phone running Android, they can do so by transferring their LBF file to that phone and opening it in the phones LG backup app. Typically, the backup app allows users to restore all the data an LBF file contains or select portions of the data. For example, LG Mobile Switch allows a user to restore their personal data, media data, and/or downloaded apps. You can use LG Mobile Switch (Android) to restore the data an LBF file contains. To do so, open the app and follow its instructions for retrieving files from a backup. You can also use LBFtool (multiplatform) to extract the files an LBF file contains. Windows LBFtool. Mac LBFtool. Linux LBFtool. Android LG Mobile Switch. LG Backup —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows LBFtool. Mac LBFtool. Linux LBFtool. Android LG Mobile Switch. LG Backup —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".NOY",
    "NOY Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "A NOY file is a backup file created by NOY Backup Utility, a program used to create compressed backups of files. It contains one or more files or drives that have been compressed with Zip compression to reduce storage space. NOY files allow users to backup important files to protect them in case the files become corrupt or lost. The NOY file is the primary file type associated with NOY Backup Utility, which enables you to create and open NOY files. Windows NOY Backup Utility.",
    "Windows NOY Backup Utility.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".PDB",
    "PowerDesigner Database Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "A PDB file is a database file used by various applications, including Pegasus, Quicken, Microsoft Visual Studio, and Palm Pilot software. It stores data in a structured format and is typically installed with the corresponding application. PDB files used by different programs are usually saved in different proprietary formats, meaning they can be opened only by the program they were installed with. For example, Microsoft Visual Studio will not recognize an Intuit Quicken PDB file. Visual Studio uses PDB files to store debugging information about a program, including symbol information, which is too large to be stored in the program itself. The symbol information consists of a list of all symbols in a program module with addresses, the name of the file, and the line the symbol was declared on. You can use Microsoft Visual Studio (Windows) to load information from a PDB file created by that program. This allows you to debug the program the file is associated with. You can also use Microsofts CVDump program (Windows) to read the information a Visual Studio PDB file contains. Windows Intuit Quicken. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Microsoft CVDump. Mac Intuit Quicken. Data file created in the Protein Data Bank (PDB) format; stores 3D coordinates specifying the structure of atoms within a protein or other chemical compound; used as a standard format for studying protein structures; also used by the Research Collaboratory for Structural Bioinformatics (RCSB) for studying biological macromolecules. Many Protein Data Bank files are made available through the Worldwide Protein Data Bank (wwPDB), an organization that archives macromolecules and freely distributes them. NOTE: PDB files are often viewed within a Java applet that uses Jmol, an open source molecule visualization package. PDB files are also supported by some molecular viewing browser plugins. Windows Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Microsoft Internet Explorer with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Agile Molecule Abalone —  (Discontinued). Agile Molecule Ascalaph —  (Discontinued). Mac Avogadro. Jmol. Apple Safari with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet Included with OS. Linux Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Mozilla Firefox with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Web Animated PhysicsFree. Movie project file created and used by Demo Builder, a program used to create tutorials, presentations, and demonstrations to show how software and systems work; contains recorded screen scenes, along with imported video and images. A Demo Builder movie project can be exported to a variety of formats depending on how you want to present your tutorial. Supported formats include Flash, HTML, Windows Media Video, MPEG4, and Word Document. Windows Tanida Demo Builder. Backup of a PowerDesigner database (.PDM) file; includes data saved in the database as well as references to other files; created as a backup in case the main database file needs to be restored. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner. Standard data format used by several different programs on Palm-based PDA devices; may store various types of data, such as eBooks, word processing documents, spreadsheets, databases, maps, and image files. To determine what program created a PDB file, open the file in a text editor. The Type and Creator codes should be located in the header of the file near the top of the document. Windows Palm Desktop. Fictionwise eReader. DC & Co iSilo. XnViewMP. Mac Planamesa NeoOffice. Fictionwise eReader. Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. PorDiBle txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Linux txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Android Fictionwise eReaderFree.",
    "Windows Intuit Quicken. Microsoft Visual Studio 2022. Microsoft CVDump. Mac Intuit Quicken. Windows Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Microsoft Internet Explorer with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Agile Molecule Abalone —  (Discontinued). Agile Molecule Ascalaph —  (Discontinued). Mac Avogadro. Jmol. Apple Safari with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet Included with OS. Linux Avogadro. Jmol. RasMol. Mozilla Firefox with JmolApplet or Protein Workshop applet. Web Animated Physics. Windows Tanida Demo Builder. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner. Windows Palm Desktop. Fictionwise eReader. DC & Co iSilo. XnViewMP. Mac Planamesa NeoOffice. Fictionwise eReader. Lemkesoft GraphicConverter. PorDiBle txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Linux txt2pdbdoc. XnViewMP. Android Fictionwise eReader.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".PTB",
    "Sage 50 Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "Contains bass or guitar tablatures used for bass and guitar sheet music. Windows TuxGuitar. Power Tab Editor Mac TuxGuitar. TabView Linux TuxGuitarFree. A PTB file is a backup file created by Sage 50, accounting software used to organize financial data. It contains an exact copy of the company data. PTB files are used to protect a users financial data in case of data corruption or system errors. To create the PTB file, select File → Back Up, choose your settings, and click Back Up. Then name the file, choose the save location, and click Save. To restore the PTB file, select File → Restore, follow the appropriate prompts, and finally, click Finish. You can also restore a PTB file by renaming the extension from ptb to zip since PTB are compressed with Zip compression. You can then decompress the file and copy the data from the PTB file into the appropriate subdirectory. NOTE: Sage 50 used to be known as Peachtree Accounting. Windows Sage 50. A PTB file is a backup file created by Microsoft PowerToys, a utility that allows users to customize Microsoft Windows. It contains a copy of a users PowerToys settings. Users create and load PTB files from the apps PowerToys Settings window. PTB file open in Microsoft PowerToys Microsoft PowerToys is a set of utilities that allows Windows 10 and 11 users to add and adjust Windows features. For example, PowerToys allows users to install add-ons for File Explorer, use a Color Picker to copy colors between windows, and use a Screen Ruler to measure pixels on their screen. PowerToys users can modify settings for each of the apps utilities. If a user wants to back up their settings, they can do so by opening the PowerToys Settings menu and selecting General → Backup & restore → Backup. This saves a copy of the users settings as a PTB file. Typically, PTB files are saved in the following directory: C:/​Users/​YourUserName/​Documents/​PowerToys/​Backup NOTE: PTB files are.ZIP archives that store settings as.JSON files. If you want to view the JSON files a PTB file contains, change the files extension to.zip and open it as you would any ZIP file. You can open a PTB file with Microsoft PowerToys (Windows). To do so: Place your PTB file in the ~/​PowerToys/​Backup directory and delete any other PTB files located there. Open PowerToys and, in the PowerToys Settings window, select General. Scroll to the Backup & restore section. Click Restore. PowerToys will apply the settings saved in your PTB file. Windows Microsoft PowerToysFree.",
    "Windows TuxGuitar. Power Tab Editor. Mac TuxGuitar. TabView. Linux TuxGuitar. Windows Sage 50. Windows Microsoft PowerToys.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".WBCAT",
    "Windows Backup Catalog",
    "3.3",
    "A WBCAT file is a backup information file created by Windows Backup and Restore. It is stored within a backup and contains a catalog of that backups files. Backup and Restore uses WBCAT files to restore files to the correct locations during the file restore process. Windows Backup and Restore is a backup application bundled with Windows. When you use Backup and Restore to back up your files, it creates a Catalogs directory within your backup. This directory contains a single file, GlobalCatalog.wbcat. The WBCAT file contains a list of files included in the backup and their locations at the time the backup was created. When you restore your backup, Backup and Restore uses this catalog to place copies of your backed-up files in the correct locations. NOTE: Each backup created using Backup and Restore also contains several.ZIP files. These archives contain your backed-up files. GlobalCatalog.wbcat - The name of WBCAT files created by Windows Backup and Restore. WBCAT files are not meant to be opened. Windows Backup and Restore uses WBCAT files when you restore the backup in which the file is stored. Windows Microsoft Windows Backup and Restore Included with OS.",
    "Windows Microsoft Windows Backup and Restore Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".FZA",
    "Form•Z Autosave File",
    "3.3",
    "File created by form•Z, a 3D solids and surfaces modeling program; saves a backup of a form•Z project (.FMZ file) and may be one of several autosave files created while the project is opened and being edited; can be used to restore the state of a project file if the software crashes or if the user forgets to save the project. Form•Z autosave files can be set to save after every N number of operations performed in the software. Windows AutoDesSys form•Z. Mac AutoDesSys form•Z.",
    "Windows AutoDesSys form•Z. Mac AutoDesSys form•Z.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".QUICKEN2017BACKUP",
    "Quicken 2017 Backup File",
    "3.3",
    "A QUICKEN2017BACKUP file is a backup file created by the 2017 version of Quicken financial management software. It contains all user and account data, which may include personal information, reports, settings, and transactions. The QUICKEN2017BACKUP file is designed for users looking to back up their account information from the.QUICKEN2017 file. In any event that the QUICKEN2017 file becomes corrupt or is lost, the backup file can be used to restore the information. To create a backup file in Quicken, simply select File → Save a Backup.. and choose the destination folder. To restore data from a backup file, select File → Restore a Backup.. and locate the backup file. Mac Intuit Quicken.",
    "Mac Intuit Quicken.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".ASVX",
    "Finale 2014 Auto-Saved Score",
    "3.3",
    "An ASVX file is a backup of a MakeMusic Finale musical score (.MUSX file). Composers can set Finale to automatically create ASVX backups at regular intervals. ASVX files use the extension asv.musx. ASVX file open in MakeMusic Finale MakeMusic Finale is a music notation program used to compose, edit, and play back musical scores. In Finale 2014 and later versions, these scores are saved as MUSX files. Composers can configure Finale to automatically back up any MUSX files they have open at a regular interval. Finale saves these automatically-generated backups in the following directory: ~/​Documents/​Finale Files/​Backups Each backup uses the same filename as the MUSX file from which it was created, except the backups filename ends with asv.musx. Finale users and documentation often refer to these backup files as ASVX files, even though the files use the.musx extension. How to change Finales ASVX settings Finale users can adjust how often the program creates and updates ASVX backups. To do so: Open the programs Preferences menu. Select Save from the left-hand sidebar. To begin creating ASVX files, select the Auto Save File(s) Every _ Minutes checkbox. (To stop creating them, clear the checkbox.) In the _ Minutes field, specify how often you want Finale to create/update ASVX files. NOTE: Finale 2012 and earlier versions create.ASV files instead of ASVX files. You can open an ASVX file with with MakeMusic Finale (Windows, Mac). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your ASVX file. After you open your ASVX file, you can use the File → Save As.. option to save the file as a normal MUSX file. Mac MakeMusic Finale. Windows MakeMusic Finale.",
    "Mac MakeMusic Finale. Windows MakeMusic Finale.",
    "You can use MakeMusic Finale to export the score an ASVX file contains in the following formats:.MUS - Finale 2012 Score.AIFF - Audio Interchange File Format.WAV - WAVE Audio.EPUB - Open eBook.MIDI - MIDI Music Data.MXL - Compressed MusicXML."],
    ["backup_files",
    ".QBM",
    "QuickBooks Portable Company File",
    "3.2",
    "File created by QuickBooks, a program that allows businesses to track their finances; contains a compacted version of company financial data only; used to temporarily move company financial data through email or using a small capacity external storage device. If you would like to restore a QBM portable company file, you can select File → Open or Restore Company from the application menu and then choose Restore a portable file from the dialog. You will be led through several more screens to complete the restoration process. NOTE: QBM files should not be used as full backups since they only backup company financial data. To make a full backup, create a.QBB file in QuickBooks. Windows Intuit QuickBooks Pro. Mac Intuit QuickBooks for Mac.",
    "Windows Intuit QuickBooks Pro. Mac Intuit QuickBooks for Mac.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BKP",
    "Zapback Backup File",
    "3.2",
    "Backup file that may be created by various programs; often created automatically to provide a backup in case the original file becomes corrupted; the .bkp extension is often appended to the files original extension and may need to be removed in order for the file to open correctly. Backup files most commonly use the.BAK extension. Windows Open with program that created original file Mac Open with program that created original file. Backup file created by Zapback, a simple Windows backup and restore utility; contains an uncompressed copy of the original file, but with the string  - Backup.bkp appended to the original filename. BKP files can only be used for creating backups of single files. Windows Zaplots Zapback. A BKP file is a data file created by Backup Your Mobile, a backup app for Android devices. It contains a portion of a users backup data. Backup Your Mobile uses BKP files when restoring users backups, which do not themselves have a file extension. For example, if a Backup Your Mobile user creates a backup that backs up the apps on their device, Backup Your Mobile will also create a BKP file that contains a list of those applications. Backup Your Mobile uses this list to restore the users applications, as it restores the associated backup. NOTE: Artur Jaszcyzk discontinued the Backup Your Mobile app. BKP files are not meant to be opened. However, because BKP files are plain text files, you can open and view them with any text editor. Keep in mind that editing a BKP file may prevent you from being able to restore Backup Your Mobile backups. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor Linux Leafpad. gedit. Other text editor Android Backup Your Mobile —  (Discontinued). Rhythm Software QuickEdit text editor. Aquamarine Networks Jota Text Editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "Windows Open with program that created original file. Mac Open with program that created original file. Windows Zaplots Zapback. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor. Linux Leafpad. gedit. Other text editor. Android Backup Your Mobile —  (Discontinued). Rhythm Software QuickEdit text editor. Aquamarine Networks Jota Text Editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".MPB",
    "MyPhoneExplorer Backup File",
    "3.2",
    "File created by MyPhoneExplorer, a program used for syncing desktop computers and Sony Ericsson mobile phones; contains backed up phone data for contacts and SMS messages; used for backing up and restoring contacts between mobile phones and when recovering from a mobile device error. NOTE: MPB files can be imported and exported using the MyPhoneExplorer program. Windows FJ Software MyPhoneExplorerFree.",
    "Windows FJ Software MyPhoneExplorer.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".QBX",
    "QuickBooks Accountant Transfer File",
    "3.2",
    "Accountant transfer file based off a QuickBooks company.QBW file; saves QuickBooks data in a format designed for accountants and tax preparers; entries within the QBX file cannot be modified except for adding General Journal notes. To create an Accountant Transfer File, first select Accountants Review.. from the File menu, then choose Create Accountants Copy and save the file. Windows Intuit QuickBooks Pro. Mac Intuit QuickBooks for Mac. A QBX file is a landing page file created by BLOCKS, a web program used to generate static websites. It contains the components of a BLOCKS webpage, which includes the header, content, and footer, styles, and fonts that appear on the page. QBX files store all of the components in plain text. The QBX file allows you to export and import the page you created in the Blocks program. To export the file, click the disk icon on the left toolbar and select EXPORT. This will begin an automatic download of the QBX file. To import the QBX file, click the disk icon on the left toolbar, select IMPORT, and navigate to the location of the QBX file. BLOCKS is available online and comes with a variety of features such as Google web fonts, style editors, templates and blocks, code editors, material design, and bootstrap components. NOTE: Some browsers on Windows and all browsers in macOS (OS X) will not download the QBX file when you choose to export your landing page. Instead, a new browser window will open displaying the code. If this occurs, save the webpage displayed in the new window as an.HTML file and rename the extension to .qbx. Web BLOCKS.",
    "Windows Intuit QuickBooks Pro. Mac Intuit QuickBooks for Mac. Web BLOCKS.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BCKP",
    "Ad-Aware Quarantined File",
    "3.2",
    "Archive of unsafe or questionable files detected by Ad-Aware, a malware protection program for PCs and networks; collects possible malicious files and quarantines them to a safe location; created during the auto-quarantine process. BCKP files are typically named [date] [time].bckp where [date] is the datestamp and [time] is the time the file was created. Windows Lavasoft Adaware.",
    "Windows Lavasoft Adaware.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".W01",
    "Samsung Recovery File",
    "3.2",
    "Audio wave file saved by a Yamaha SY series synthesizer such as the SY99 or SY85; may also be used by the TX16W sampler, which typically saves files with a.TXW extension. Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. A W01 file is a backup data file created by Samsung Recovery software, a program that comes with Samsung computers to backup and recover data. It contains a partial backup of a computer system that can be restored if all other necessary backup files are present. W01 files are located in the /​SamsungRecovery/​ directory. The files are saved in a proprietary format and can only be opened and restored with the Samsung Recovery software used to create them. NOTE: Samsung Recovery was originally called Recovery Solution but changed to Recovery with the release of version 6, which followed version 5.6. user1.w01 - The name of the backup file that contains a state backup. The next file will be named user1.w02, then user1.w03, and so on. init.w01 - The name of the backup that contains the factory image (formerly called initial image), which is an image used to restore the computers original factory firmware and settings. Windows Samsung Recovery Included with OS.",
    "Windows FMJ-Software Awave Studio. Windows Samsung Recovery Included with OS.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".GB2",
    "Game Maker Backup File",
    "3.2",
    "Backup file created by GameMaker: Studio, a game development application for Windows; created as a backup of the original project file. You can open a GB2 file by using the import function in GameMaker: Studio. First, select File → Import Project.. and then, choose your file. Windows YoYo Games GameMaker: Studio.",
    "Windows YoYo Games GameMaker: Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".TIBKP",
    "Titanium Backup File",
    "3.2",
    "Backup file created by Titanium Backup, an application used to back up files on Android devices; contains a backup of an app with related data or just the data itself; stored locally and can be exported to other devices. To import a TIBKP file, press the menu button, select import backup (TiBkp), and choose the TIBKP file you want to import. NOTE: Titanium Backup is available for free. Titanium Backup PRO, which must be purchased, unlocks additional features. Android Titanium Track Titanium BackupFree.",
    "Android Titanium Track Titanium Backup.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".PBF",
    "Paragon Backup File",
    "3.1",
    "Backup archive created by one of Paragons backup and recovery applications; stores backup files in a proprietary format; can be browsed within the software, which enables users to restore individual files or a whole file system. In addition to system backups, PBF files are often used for migrating Windows file systems between versions of Windows operating systems. Windows Paragon Backup & Recovery Suite. Paragon System Backup. Backup archive created by CyberLink PowerBackup, a backup and recovery application; stores a collection of backed up files and folders; can be used for full, differential, or incremental backup strategies; used for restoring files through the PowerBackup application. PowerBackup can create backups on a periodic basis through its job scheduler component, which uses.PBJ job files. Windows CyberLink PowerBackup. Contains audio samples that can be loaded into Turtle Beach audio software or external synthesizers; references.WAV files that must be stored in the same directory. Windows Voyetra Turtle Beach Pinnacle Project Studio FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "Windows Paragon Backup & Recovery Suite. Paragon System Backup. Windows CyberLink PowerBackup. Windows Voyetra Turtle Beach Pinnacle Project Studio FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".NBAK",
    "Neat Backup File",
    "3.1",
    "Backup file created by Neat 5, a digital filing system application; contains a backup of your scanned documents, including receipts and contacts; similar to the.NRBAK and.NWBAK files. To create a NBAK file, select Tools → Database → Offline Backup, click Browse, choose the save location (Dont select the Neat Data folder location), click Backup to begin the process, set a backup reminder if youd like, and click Save + Close. To restore a database using the NBAK file, select Tools → Database → Offline Restore, navigate to your file, and click Open. Windows Neat.",
    "Windows Neat.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BK1",
    "Autodesk Backup File",
    "3.1",
    "Backup file created by Autodesk products, including AutoCAD Mechanical, Mechanical Desktop, and AutoCAD Map; stores a.BAK file that has been renamed with the .bk1 extension; renamed when the Autodesk program terminates unexpectedly. BAK files are automatically created when users save drawing files. Therefore, when a program crashes, Autodesk applications try to rename the BAK file to BK1 to prevent a corrupted drawing file from replacing the original backup. NOTE: If the BK1 extension is already in use, Autodesk programs use .bk2 through .bk9, as well as .bka through .bkz and .baa through .bzz until a unique extension is found. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Autodesk AutoCAD Mechanical 2023. File created by Indexing Service, a component of Windows used to automatically index file system search information; contains information used for making fast file searches in Windows; typically seen with the name propstor.bk1. BK1 files are often located within the C:/​System Volume Information/​catalog.wci/​ directory. Other catalog index files in this directory may include.BK2,.PS1,.PS2,.FID,.000, and.HSH files. NOTE: Windows may also create BK1 files on external drives, such as USB flash drives. Windows Microsoft Windows. Backup file created by ERwin Data Modeler, a data modeling program; contains a backup of a.ER1 diagram file; created automatically by ERwin when the ER1 file is opened; used to recover a data model file if the original becomes corrupted. BK1 files are used by older versions of ERwin Data Modeler. Windows CA ERwin Data Modeler.",
    "Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023. Autodesk AutoCAD Mechanical 2023. Windows Microsoft Windows. Windows CA ERwin Data Modeler.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".FLKA",
    "Folder Lock Portable Locker File",
    "3.1",
    "Encrypted archive created by Folder Lock, a program used for backing up sensitive data into lockers; stores an encrypted archive of files and can only be opened with the password set by the user; uses FAT32 file system formatting and supports up to 4GB file sizes; can be backed up to the NewSoftwares online backup service for remote backup and recovery; can also be written to external drives or CD/DVDs. FLKA files are referred to as Portable Lockers. Folder Lock also supports Basic Lockers (.FLKB extension), which do not have the 4GB file size limit, but they cannot be used with NewSoftwares online backup service. NOTE: The FLKA and FLKB extensions were introduced with Folder Lock 7. Prior versions of the software use.FLK files for lockers. Windows NewSoftwares Folder Lock.",
    "Windows NewSoftwares Folder Lock.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".113",
    "Iomega Backup File",
    "3.1",
    "Backup of data typically stored on an Iomega removable storage device. Windows Iomega Backup Mac Iomega Backup.",
    "Windows Iomega Backup. Mac Iomega Backup.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BBB",
    "BlackBerry Mobile Phone Backup File",
    "3.0",
    "Backup file created by the Mac version of BlackBerry Desktop Manager, a program used for syncing, backing up, and restoring data with BlackBerry mobile devices; stores contacts, the calendar, applications, and other data from the device. BBB files can be used to restore the state of a BlackBerry device or to transfer states between BlackBerry phones. Windows Reincubate BlackBerry Backup Extractor. BlackBerry Desktop Software. Mac Research In Motion BlackBerry Desktop Manager. BlackBerry Desktop SoftwareFree.",
    "Windows Reincubate BlackBerry Backup Extractor. BlackBerry Desktop Software. Mac Research In Motion BlackBerry Desktop Manager. BlackBerry Desktop Software.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BK",
    "Smart Switch Backup",
    "3.0",
    "A BK file contains a book created with Adobe FrameMaker, a program used to author, enrich, manage, and publish technical documentation. It contains pages that are formatted for print and may include text as well as raster and bitmap images. BK files were replaced with.BOOK files by FrameMaker. You most likely will only encounter BK book files if you use early versions of Adobe FrameMaker to compose technical documents. The purpose of BK book files is to organize multiple pages (stored in.FM files) into one composition, much like a real-life book. While books are an important aspect of FrameMaker, BK files are no longer commonly used by the software for saving books. In the mid-1990s, FrameMaker began saving books in version 5 with the.book file extension instead of the.bk file extension. NOTE: Since the BK format is old and deprecated you should save your books in FrameMaker as BOOK files instead of BK files. Windows Adobe FrameMaker. Linux Adobe FrameMaker. SmartSwitchBackup.bk is a backup control file included in a backup created by Samsung Smart Switch. It contains data used to restore a users data to a Samsung Galaxy phone. SmartSwitchBackup.bk is not meant to be manually opened by users. Samsung Smart Switch is the official backup app used to transfer a users contacts, photos, settings, call history, and other data from one Samsung Galaxy phone to another. Each Smart Switch backup contains several folders that contain encrypted files (such as.SNMM and.EXML files). Each backup also includes a BK file named SmartSwitchBackup.bk. SmartSwitchBackup.bk is the central file Samsung Smart Switch uses to restore the data a users Smart Switch backup contains. NOTE: Some versions of Samsung Smart Switch and Samsung Kies (a previous Samsung backup application) produce additional BK files, which contain specific subsets of your backup data. SmartSwitchBackup.bk is not meant to be manually opened. You can use Samsung Smart Switch (Android, Windows, Mac) to restore a backup that contains a BK file(s) to your Samsung Galaxy device. You can also use MOBILedit Forensic Express (Windows) to load and browse a backup that contains a BK file(s). Windows Samsung Smart Switch. MOBILedit Forensic Express. Oxygen Forensics Detective. Mac Samsung Smart Switch. Android Samsung Smart SwitchFree.",
    "Windows Adobe FrameMaker. Linux Adobe FrameMaker. Windows Samsung Smart Switch. MOBILedit Forensic Express. Oxygen Forensics Detective. Mac Samsung Smart Switch. Android Samsung Smart Switch.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".AEA",
    "AdWords Editor Archive",
    "3.0",
    "Contains settings for an alarm created with Ae Timer, an alarm clock and scheduling program; includes the alarm time, alarm text, and the song or video that is played for the alarm; can be edited and saved by the user. Windows Ae Applications Ae Timer. Backup archive created by Google AdWords Editor, an application used to manage information for Google AdWords advertising campaigns; contains the advertising data for the campaign; used for creating full or partial backups. AEA files may store data for an entire account or select Ad Groups and Campaigns. You can export one of these options by selecting File → Export Backup (AEA) and then choosing one of the submenu items. NOTE: AEA files are also used by Google Translator Toolkit, a browser-based application that can automatically translate the advertising campaign information into other languages. Windows Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Mac Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Linux Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). An AEA file contains audio data encoded in the ATRAC1 format, which is a data compression format developed by Sony. It stores audio most likely dumped from a MiniDisc (MD), which is an optical disc similar to a compact disc (CD) that can be played with various MD players. AEA files are not common, since MDs were introduced back in 1992 and overshadowed by CDs. You will most likely never encounter an AEA file unless you dump audio from an MD you own. You may also receive an AEA file from a friend sharing music dumped from one of his MDs. The ATRAC1 format is a variation of the ATRAC format, which stands for Adaptive TRansform Acoustic Coding. Besides being used in MDs, the format was also utilized in the Sony Dynamic Digital Sound (SDDS) theater sound system in the 1990s. Since AEA files are uncommon, there are few media players that support them. However, you can convert AEA files to a more widely supported audio format with FFmpeg, then play the converted file with a media player, such as Microsoft Windows Media Player or VideoLAN VLC media player. Unless the AEA file stores audio you cannot get anywhere else, such as a recorded narration or rare music recording, it is most likely easier to re-purchase or stream the audio from a digital music service than to convert it to a more common format that can be played. Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpegFree.",
    "Windows Ae Applications Ae Timer. Windows Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Mac Google AdWords Editor. Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Linux Google Translator Toolkit —  (Discontinued). Windows File Viewer Plus — Get it from Microsoft. FFmpeg. Mac FFmpeg. Linux FFmpeg.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".JWLIBRARY",
    "JW Library Backup",
    "3.0",
    "A JWLIBRARY file is a backup file created by JW Library, an eReader used to read Jehovahs Witnesses Publications. It contains a users document annotations, including notes and highlighting. JWLIBRARY files do not contain a backup of the books and other documents a user has stored in JW Library. JW Library is a mobile and Windows application that allows users to import and read Jehovahs Witnesses publications on their smartphone, tablet, or PC. For example, users can download, import, and read documents saved as.JWPUB files. While reading, JW Library users can annotate documents with notes, highlighting, underlines, bookmarks, and tags. If a user wants to back up these annotations, they can do so by clicking JW Librarys Cloud icon and selecting Create a backup. This saves the users annotations as a JWLIBRARY file, which they can store on their device, send to a cloud storage service, or email to themself. You can import a JWLIBRARY file into JW Library (Windows, Android, iOS) to restore the annotations it contains. To do so: Open JW Library and select the Cloud icon. Select Restore a backup. Navigate to and import your JWLIBRARY file. Advanced users can use JWLMerge (Windows) to merge the annotations two or more JWLIBRARY files contain into a single JWLIBRARY file, which can then be used to restore the merged annotations in JW Library. Windows JW Library. JWLMerge. iOS JW Library. Android JW LibraryFree.",
    "Windows JW Library. JWLMerge. iOS JW Library. Android JW Library.",
    "?"],
