    ["backup_files",
    ".PBF",
    "PowerBackup Data File",
    "2.9",
    "Backup archive created by one of Paragons backup and recovery applications; stores backup files in a proprietary format; can be browsed within the software, which enables users to restore individual files or a whole file system. In addition to system backups, PBF files are often used for migrating Windows file systems between versions of Windows operating systems. Windows Paragon Backup & Recovery Suite. Paragon System Backup. Backup archive created by CyberLink PowerBackup, a backup and recovery application; stores a collection of backed up files and folders; can be used for full, differential, or incremental backup strategies; used for restoring files through the PowerBackup application. PowerBackup can create backups on a periodic basis through its job scheduler component, which uses.PBJ job files. Windows CyberLink PowerBackup. Contains audio samples that can be loaded into Turtle Beach audio software or external synthesizers; references.WAV files that must be stored in the same directory. Windows Voyetra Turtle Beach Pinnacle Project Studio FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "Windows Paragon Backup & Recovery Suite. Paragon System Backup. Windows CyberLink PowerBackup. Windows Voyetra Turtle Beach Pinnacle Project Studio FMJ-Software Awave Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".EXML",
    "Smart Switch Backup Encrypted XML File",
    "2.9",
    "An EXML file is an XML file that contains settings for No Mans Sky, an exploration and survival video game. No Mans Sky modders create and use EXML files to modify the games gameplay, using NMS Modding Station. You can open and edit an EXML file in any text editor. No Mans Sky stores all its game assets in.PAK files. Enterprising No Mans Sky modders have created programs that allow them to extract, convert, and edit these files. One such program is NMS Modding Station. NMS Modding Station converts many of No Man Skys PAK files into.MBIN files. These are binary files that contain No Man Skys general gameplay settings, as well as settings used to generate items and determine how in-game objects behave. To edit these settings, modders must first convert the binary MBIN files into plain text EXML files. Then, modders can edit No Mans Skys settings using any text editor. After editing EXML files, modders convert the files back into PAK files and repack them in No Mans Sky, to apply their edits to the games settings. You can open an EXML file and edit the No Mans Sky settings it contains in any text or source code editor, such as Microsoft Visual Studio Code (cross-platform). After youve finished editing the settings your EXML file contains, you can use NMS Modding Station (Windows) to convert your EXML file back into a PAK file and install it as a No Mans Sky mod. Windows NMS Modding Station. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Linux Vim. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS. An EXML file is an encrypted XML file created by Samsung Smart Switch, a backup app for Samsung Galaxy phones. It contains a portion of a Samsung Galaxy backup, such as a record of a users settings or call log. EXML files can be converted to normal.XML files using Wondershare MobileTrans. Samsung Smart Switch is the official backup app used to transfer a users contacts, photos, settings, call history, and other data from one Samsung Galaxy phone to another. When creating a backup, Smart Switch creates several encrypted files, each of which contains a portion of the users phone data. Smart Switch then stores the encrypted files in a Smart Switch/​Backup folder on the users phone or PC. Some of the files that a Smart Switch backup contains are EXML files. These files are XML files that have been encrypted, typically using an encryption key based on the users PIN. EXML files contain a record of a users settings, backup file lists, and call logs. Because they are encrypted, EXML files cannot be opened in a text editor like normal XML files. To view the data an EXML file contains, you must first decrypt the file. You can use Wondershare MobileTrans (Windows, Mac) to decrypt your EXML files. To do so, open MobileTrans and point it at the folder that contains your EXML files. You may have to specify that your backup is a Kies backup file, as MobileTrans does not yet officially recognize Smart Switchs Galaxy backup format. Then, run MobileTranss transfer process. After you do, your Smart Switch/​Backup folder should contain a new DecryptData sub-folder, which contains a decrypted version of your EXML file. You can open the decrypted version of your EXML file in any text editor, as you would any other XML file. You can also use Samsung Smart Switch (Android, Windows, Mac) to transfer the data your EXML file contains to a Galaxy smartphone, as part of the normal Galaxy backup and restore process. Windows Wondershare MobileTrans. Samsung Smart Switch. Mac Wondershare MobileTrans. Samsung Smart Switch. Android Samsung Smart SwitchFree.",
    "Windows NMS Modding Station. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Linux Vim. Microsoft Visual Studio Code. Any text editor. Chrome OS Google Chrome Text Included with OS. Windows Wondershare MobileTrans. Samsung Smart Switch. Mac Wondershare MobileTrans. Samsung Smart Switch. Android Samsung Smart Switch.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BPB",
    "PowerDesigner Business Process Backup File",
    "2.9",
    "Backup copy of a Business Process Model (.BPM) file created with Sybase PowerDesigner; automatically created with a model or multi-model report is saved; can be used to restore the Process Model if the original file cannot be used. Windows Sybase PowerDesigner.",
    "Windows Sybase PowerDesigner.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".ACR",
    "Acer eRecovery Management Backup File",
    "2.8",
    "Script created with ACRobot (AutoCursorRobot), a program that creates scripts for mouse and keyboard actions; used for automating common tasks and speeding up repetitive jobs. ACR files are created using ACRobots built-in scripting language. However, they are recorded based on the users actions and do not require any manual programming. Windows Acr-Soft ACRobot. File generated by Image Comparer, a program used for identifying duplicate audio files on the hard drive; saves the results of comparing audio files (i.e., songs and music) with each other; enables users to review the comparisons later without having to re-process them again. Windows Bolide Audio Comparer. Full system backup created with Acers eRecovery Management tool, a backup utility included with Acer computers; contains the entire contents of a hard disk, including both the system and user files. ACR files can be burned to a CD or DVD and can be used to restore an entire system using the eRecovery Management program. Windows Acer eRecovery Management. Medical image file format used by the National Electrical Manufacturers Association (ACR-NEMA); stores an image taken by radiological equipment; used to store patient records in a digital format. The.DCM file format is more commonly used to store radiological images. Windows AMIDE XnViewMP. Mac AMIDE XnViewMP. Linux AMIDE XnViewMPFree.",
    "Windows Acr-Soft ACRobot. Windows Bolide Audio Comparer. Windows Acer eRecovery Management. Windows AMIDE XnViewMP. Mac AMIDE XnViewMP. Linux AMIDE XnViewMP.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".SME",
    "Samsung Mobile Backup File",
    "2.8",
    "An SME file is a backup file created by Samsung backup programs, such as Kies and Smart Switch. It stores an archive of backup data for your mobile phone, which includes short text (SMS) messages and memos. SME files are similar to.SBU backup files. Samsung Kies software comes bundled with Samsung phones. The SME file can be viewed in Kies and imported into a Samsung mobile device that is supported by the Kies application. Samsung Smart Switch is also available to restore and backup data in Samsung mobile phones. Smart Switch is available for Windows, macOS, and Android. Android Samsung Smart Switch Mobile. Windows Samsung Kies. Samsung Smart Switch. Mac Samsung Kies. Samsung Smart SwitchFree. Encrypted file created by Smart Soft SmartEncryptor, a file and folder encryption and decryption application; contains a secured file that can only be viewed when decrypted in SmartEncryptor by entering the password. To encrypt your file, therefore replacing the current extension with the SME extension, select the Encrypt tab, click Add Files, navigate to your file, click OK, enter and confirm the password you want for your SME file, and click Encrypt, choose the save location, name the file, and click Save. To decrypt your SME file, select the Decrypt tab, click Browse, navigate to your file, click Open, enter your password, select a destination folder for the decrypted file, and click OK. NOTE: Smart Soft SmartEncryptor is no longer available for download. Windows Smart Soft SmartEncryptor.",
    "Android Samsung Smart Switch Mobile. Windows Samsung Kies. Samsung Smart Switch. Mac Samsung Kies. Samsung Smart Switch. Windows Smart Soft SmartEncryptor.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".ASV",
    "Finale 2012 Auto-Saved Score",
    "2.8",
    "An ASV file is an autosave file created by MathWorks MATLAB, a mathematical analysis and computation program. It contains an automatically saved version of a MATLAB source code file, better known as an.M file. By default, ASV files are stored in the same location as the M files from which they are created. MATLAB includes an Editor/Debugger that researchers, developers, and engineers use to create M files. If you edit an M file in the MATLAB Editor/Debugger and do not save your edits within the span of five minutes, MATLAB creates an autosaved version of your edited file. That version is saved with the.asv file extension. If MATLAB quits unexpectedly while you are editing an M file, you can open the corresponding ASV file to keep working from the most recently autosaved version of your file. If you want to adjust how MATLAB creates ASV files, you can do so by opening the programs Preferences menu and selecting Editor/Debugger → Autosave. From this menu, you can specify how often MATLAB autosaves files, what extension MATLAB assigns to autosaved files, and where autosaves are stored. NOTE: On Linux and other Unix platforms, MATLAB assigns the.m~ extension to autosaves. You can open an ASV file with the MathWorks MATLAB Editor/Debugger just as you would any M file. If you need a reminder of where your ASV files are stored, open the MATLAB Preferences menu (File → Preferences) and select Editor/Debugger → Autosave to view the location in which MATLAB stores autosaves. Windows The MathWorks MATLAB. Mac The MathWorks MATLAB. Linux The MathWorks MATLAB. An ASV file is an auto-saved backup of a MakeMusic Finale musical score. Users can set Finale to create ASV files at regular intervals, to automatically back up their work. ASV files use the extension asv.mus. ASV file open in MakeMusic Finale MakeMusic Finale is a music notation program that composers use to create, edit, and play back musical scores. In Finale 2012 and earlier versions, these scores are saved as.MUS files. Optionally, composers can configure Finale to automatically back up open MUS files at a regular interval, so they dont lose their work if the program closes unexpectedly. Finale saves these automatically-generated backups in the following directory: ~/​Documents/​Finale Files/​Backups Each backup uses the same filename as the MUS file from which it was created, except that the backups filename ends with asv.mus, to note it is an auto-saved backup. Finale users and documentation often refer to these backup files as ASV files, even though the files use the.mus extension. How to change Finales auto-save settings Finale users can adjust how often the program creates and updates ASV backups. To do so: Open Finales Preferences menu. Select Save from the left-hand sidebar. To begin creating ASV files, select the Auto Save File(s) Every _ Minutes checkbox. (To stop creating them, clear the checkbox.) In the _ Minutes field, specify how often you want Finale to create/update ASV files. NOTE: Finale 2014 and later versions create.ASVX files instead of ASV files. You can open an ASV file with MakeMusic Finale (Windows, Mac). To do so, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your ASV file. After you open your ASV file, you can use the File → Save As.. option to save the file as a normal MUS or.MUSX file. Windows MakeMusic Finale. Mac MakeMusic Finale. Color settings file used by Adobe Photoshop, a program used to create and edit raster graphics; contains color adjustment settings for cyan, magenta, yellow, and black (CMYK) values of different colors, which are on a scale from -100% to +100%); also contains the selective color method, which is either relative or absolute; used for saving color adjustment presets that can be applied to multiple images. The Selective Color window can be accessed in Photoshop by selecting Image → Adjustments → Selective Color... Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023.",
    "Windows The MathWorks MATLAB. Mac The MathWorks MATLAB. Linux The MathWorks MATLAB. Windows MakeMusic Finale. Mac MakeMusic Finale. Windows Adobe Photoshop 2023. Mac Adobe Photoshop 2023.",
    "You can use MakeMusic Finale to export the score an ASV file contains in a variety of formats, including:.AIFF - Audio Interchange File Format.WAV - WAVE Audio.EPUB - Open eBook.MIDI - MIDI Music Data.MXL - Compressed MusicXML."],
    ["backup_files",
    ".JDC",
    "JDownloader Links File",
    "2.8",
    "Backup file created by JDownlaoder, a Java-based program used to manage Internet downloads; contains a collection of links that were used for downloading files; used for backing up download locations so they can be transferred to another system or recovered in the case of lost data. Windows JDownloader. Mac JDownloader. Linux JDownloaderFree.",
    "Windows JDownloader. Mac JDownloader. Linux JDownloader.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".YRCBCK",
    "Weblink Backup",
    "2.8",
    "A YRCBCK file is a backup file created by YRC Group Weblink, a web browser for Windows. It contains a copy of a users history, bookmark archive files (.YRCBKM files), saved form information, and settings. Weblink users can load a YRCBCK file to import their data into another instance of Weblink. YRCBCK file open in YRC Group Weblink Weblink is a web browser that was published by the Indian company YRC Group, which has since become Yash Impacts. YRC Group discontinued Weblink in 2014, but the program is still available for download from Yash Impacts website. Users can save a copy of their Weblink data to a YRCBCK file. This allows them to back up their data and reload it if, for example, they are forced to reinstall Weblink. To create a YRCBCK file in Weblink: From Weblinks menu, select Start Backup Manager. From the YRC Backup Manager window, select Make a Backup. Select the Weblink data you want to save. Then, select Make backup. The YRCBCK file will be saved with a filename that uses the format backup-dd-mm-yy.yrcbck. This allows you to quickly see when the file was created. You can import the data a YRCBCK file contains into YRC Group Weblink (Windows). To do so: From Weblinks menu, select Start Backup Manager. From the YRC Backup Manager window, select Restore a Backup. Select the.. button, then navigate to and open your YRCBCK file. Select the information you want to import. Select Restore. Windows YRC Group WeblinkFree.",
    "Windows YRC Group Weblink.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".NBI",
    "Nero BackItUp Information File",
    "2.7",
    "File created by BackItUp (formerly BackItUp & Burn), a program used to compress and backup files; contains information about files that have been backed up; used in conjunction with.NBA files to restore from a backed up archive. Windows Nero BackItUp.",
    "Windows Nero BackItUp.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".TIS",
    "True Image Script",
    "2.7",
    "A TIS file is a backup script used by Acronis Windows backup software including True Image and Backup & Recovery. It saves a series of commands used for automating backup tasks. TIS files are often used by system administrators for scheduling backups in enterprise environments. NOTE: In September 2021, Acronis renamed True Image to Cyber Protect Home Office. Windows Acronis Cyber Protect Home Office.",
    "Windows Acronis Cyber Protect Home Office.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".XBK",
    "XenServer Backup File",
    "2.7",
    "Backup file created by Citrix virtualization software; saves the configuration for a virtual server host so that it can be restored and restarted if it unexpectedly quits; does not include the virtual machines running on the server. XBK files can be created (and restored) by XenServer or XenClient, a Windows GUI used for managing XenServer hosts. Windows Citrix XenCenter. Citrix XenServer. File created by SMART Notebook software, a program used to create and deliver classroom lessons; may contain images, notes, diagrams, audio, and video; used for storing and distributing classroom notes; can be exported to.HTML or.PDF files in SMART Notebook software. XBK files can be converted to the newer.NOTEBOOK format in more recent versions of SMART Notebook software. Windows SMART Technologies Notebook. SMART Technologies Board software Mac SMART Technologies Notebook. SMART Technologies Board software Linux SMART Technologies Notebook.",
    "Windows Citrix XenCenter. Citrix XenServer. Windows SMART Technologies Notebook. SMART Technologies Board software. Mac SMART Technologies Notebook. SMART Technologies Board software. Linux SMART Technologies Notebook.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".PBB",
    "AT&T Phonebook File",
    "2.7",
    "Phonebook file used by various mobile phones; contains backup data exported by software at a local AT&T store; typically stored on a USB drive after an AT&T representative has exported the phonebook file. PBB files can be opened using CellBrite Content Manager by selecting Contacts → Open Phonebook. They may then be exported to Outlook or Outlook Express by selecting the menu option Contacts → Open Phonebook. Windows CellBrite Mobile Synchronization Content Manager. A PBB file is a VEX V5 robot design created by Protobot Beta, a VEX V5 prototyping tool. It contains a 3D model comprised of VEX V5 elements. VEX V5 users can save and share PBB files with each other to distribute robot designs. VEX V5 is an educational robotics system that teachers use to teach high school and college students about engineering and coding. Students can use the VEX V5 system to construct robots that solve problems or compete in competitions. Protobot Beta is an unofficial tool that VEX V5 users can use to prototype robots on their PC, before attempting to build them in real life. This allows robot creators to test their robots and share their robot designs with other VEX V5 users. You can open a PBB file with Protobot Beta (Windows). To do so, select File → Open from the programs menu bar. Then, navigate to and open your PBB file. Windows Protobot BetaFree.",
    "Windows CellBrite Mobile Synchronization Content Manager. Windows Protobot Beta.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".NBS",
    "NTI Backup Set",
    "2.7",
    "An NBS file contains an audio project created by Minecraft Note Block Studio (NBS) or Open NBS, which are third-party programs used to create custom Minecraft music. It contains note blocks organized to be played as an in-game song. NBS files also contain song metadata, including the songs name, author, and length. You can open an NBS file with Open Note Block Studio (Windows) or Minecraft Note Block Studio (Windows). Open Note Block Studio is actively maintained, while Minecraft Note Block Studio is not. Windows Open Note Block Studio. Minecraft Note Block Studio —  (Discontinued). Backup file created by NTI Backup Now, a backup and restore program for Windows; references a corresponding NTI Backup File (.NBF extension), which contains the backup data; used for saving and loading the backup set. NBS files differ from.NPS files, which are hard drive partition backup sets. An NBS backup is called a File-Based Backup in NTI Backup Now, while an NPF backup is called a Drive-Based Backup.. Windows NTI Backup Now.",
    "Windows Open Note Block Studio. Minecraft Note Block Studio —  (Discontinued). Windows NTI Backup Now.",
    "NBS file open in Open Note Block Studio In Minecraft, note blocks are blocks that play musical notes when attacked or powered by redstone. Minecraft modders can use either version of NBS to create custom Minecraft songs, which are meant to be played by: Importing them as a group of note blocks Using custom commands (with cheats enabled) Each NBS project is saved as an NBS file. This file lists the note blocks a song uses as well as what notes those blocks play. Users can play the song an NBS file contains in either version of NBS. Users can also export the song as a:.MP3,.WAV,.AIFF, or.FLAC file MCEdit.SCHEMATIC file Minecraft data pack Exporting a song as an MP3, WAV, AIFF, or FLAC file allows users to play it in any common media player. Exporting a song as a SCHEMATIC file or data pack allows users to import the song into a Minecraft world. NOTE: Minecraft Note Block Studio can import.MID files. Minecraft users often use this feature to convert their favorite MIDI songs into Minecraft music."],
    ["backup_files",
    ".QBK",
    "QuickTax Backup File",
    "2.7",
    "Backup file created by QuickTax, a program used to file Canadian tax returns; contains a copy of a corresponding.Q08 or.Q09 tax return file; auto-saved by default each time a tax return file is saved. NOTE: If a Q08 or Q09 file becomes corrupted, users may rename the QBK file extension from .qbk to .q08 or .q09 and open it. By default, QBK files are saved in the following directory, where xxx is the year: Documents and Settings/​User/​My Documents/​QuickTax/​2xxx NOTE: In 2011, Intuit Canada changed the name of QuickTax to TurboTax. Windows Intuit Canada TurboTax. Intuit Canada QuickTax Mac Intuit Canada TurboTax. Intuit Canada QuickTax.",
    "Windows Intuit Canada TurboTax. Intuit Canada QuickTax. Mac Intuit Canada TurboTax. Intuit Canada QuickTax.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".PQB",
    "Pleco Chinese Dictionary Backup File",
    "2.7",
    "Backup file used by Pleco Chinese Dictionary, a Chinese document reader, dictionary, and flashcard program for iOS; stores a backup of a user dictionary or flashcard database; may contain a Websters English or Oxford E-C dictionary. To create a user dictionary from a PQB file, select Settings → Manage Dictionaries from the SETTINGS tab in the Navigation pane and click Add User. Then locate and choose your PQB file. PQB files are similar to.PQB-BACKUP files that are used by older versions of Pleco Chinese Dictionary. NOTE: When backing up and restoring PQB files that contain flashcards, be sure to select the Backup Database and Restore Database commands instead of Export Cards and Import Cards.. iOS Pleco Chinese Dictionary 3.",
    "iOS Pleco Chinese Dictionary 3.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".ORI",
    "Original File",
    "2.6",
    "Often added to a file that already has an extension; may be appended to the filename, i.e. page1.html may become page1.html.ori; often used to differentiate between original and backup (.BAK) files. The .ori extension may need to be removed in order for the file to open correctly. Windows Open with the program that created the file Mac Open with the program that created the file.",
    "Windows Open with the program that created the file. Mac Open with the program that created the file.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".__B",
    "File Splitter & Joiner Encrypted Archive File",
    "2.6",
    "Encrypted split archive file created by File Splitter & Joiner (FFSJ), a spanned archive application; stores the second part of a multi-part encrypted archive; enables users to store password-protected data in smaller segments. FFSJ uses the extensions .__a, .__b, .__c,.., ._aa, ._ab, etc. when creating encrypted split archives. The application uses .001, .002, etc. for unencrypted archives. Windows File Splitter & Joiner —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows File Splitter & Joiner —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".BBZ",
    "BerryBuzz Backup File",
    "2.6",
    "Backup file created by BerryBuzz, a program used for assigning LED colors for handheld BlackBerry devices; saves a backup of the LED configuration data and is stored on the BlackBerrys media card; can be transferred to the PC and viewed with a text editor. Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "Windows Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".NBD",
    "NovaBACKUP File",
    "2.6",
    "Backup file created by Data Backup Windows backup software; may include user and system files; uses compression to reduce the file size; may be created manually by the user in Data Backup or from a.NBK backup job. Prosoft Engineering Data Backup PC has been discontinued. Windows Prosoft Engineering Data Backup PC. Backup file format introduced with version 10 of NovaBACKUP, a backup and restore utility for Windows; saves the backup data for the backup job, which can include user and system files; saved in a compressed format and can only be opened by NovaBACKUP. Windows NovaStor NovaBACKUP Professional 17.",
    "Windows Prosoft Engineering Data Backup PC. Windows NovaStor NovaBACKUP Professional 17.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".ASHBAK",
    "Ashampoo Backup Archive",
    "2.6",
    "Backup file created by Ashampoo Burning Studio, a backup and recovery and disc burning application; contains all backed up file contents; commonly used for archiving data such as digital photos, music, and professional work. Windows Ashampoo Burning Studio.",
    "Windows Ashampoo Burning Studio.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".DNA",
    "CA Backup and Migration Backup File",
    "2.5",
    "A DNA file is a data file created by GSL Biotech SnapGene, a molecular biology analysis application. It stores a DNA sequence and includes metadata, such as the author, a description of the sequence, and comments. DNA file open in GSL Biotech SnapGene 6 GSL Biotech SnapGene is a molecular biology program that documents, designs, and simulates DNA sequences. When you save a DNA sequence, the software creates a DNA file to store the contents. To create a DNA file with SnapGene, follow these steps: Select File → New DNA or RNA File.. Choose the DNA sequence type Create the sequence Name the file Select OK After creating the DNA file, you can save it by selecting File → Save or Save As.. Then, after saving the file, you can close it and re-open it to modify the sequence further. You can open a DNA file with GSL Biotech SnapGene (multiplatform). To open a DNA file with SnapGene, select File → Open Files.. You can also open a DNA file with SnapGene Viewer in Windows and macOS. However, it does not provide the same extensive capabilities that SnapGene offers. Windows GSL Biotech SnapGene. GSL Biotech SnapGene Viewer. Mac GSL Biotech SnapGene. GSL Biotech SnapGene Viewer. Linux GSL Biotech SnapGene. GSL Biotech SnapGene ViewerFree. File created by CA Backup and Migration, a program used to backup a computers DNA; contains network, printer, system, and application settings as well as files, folders, address books, and photos; used for backing up computer settings and transferring settings from one computer to another. DNA files are self-extractable. When opened, they automatically migrate the backed up settings and files to the new computer. Windows CA Backup and Migration CA Desktop DNA Migrator. Data file used by GenePool, an artificial life simulation game; contains the DNA for a creature that can be simulated with other creatures in a virtual experiment; sometimes used for competitions to see which players custom creatures survive better than others when simulated together. NOTE: DNA files are also used by Darwin Pond, the predecessor to GenePool. However, Darwin Pond DNA files use a plain text format while GenePool DNA files use binary formatting. The Darwin Pond DNA files contain a fixed list of parameters separated by line breaks, and each file has the same file size. Windows GenePool. Rocket Science Games Darwin PondFree.",
    "Windows GSL Biotech SnapGene. GSL Biotech SnapGene Viewer. Mac GSL Biotech SnapGene. GSL Biotech SnapGene Viewer. Linux GSL Biotech SnapGene. GSL Biotech SnapGene Viewer. Windows CA Backup and Migration CA Desktop DNA Migrator. Windows GenePool. Rocket Science Games Darwin Pond.",
    "GSL Biotech SnapGene can convert DNA files to various file types, including the following formats:.SEQ - DNA Sequence Text File.FA - FASTA Sequence File.EMBL - EMBL Sequence Data File.GBK - GenBank Data File.TXT - Plain Text File.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics File.PDF - Portable Document Format."],
    ["backup_files",
    ".MYNOTESBACKUP",
    "Keep My Notes Backup",
    "2.5",
    "A MYNOTESBACKUP file contains a backup of notes created by Keep My Notes, a notepad and memo app for Android devices. It stores a backup of one or more notes, which include text, font color and size, and the theme style. MYNOTESBACKUP files are useful for saving a backup of important notes and transferring notes between devices. To create a MYNOTESBACKUP file in Keep My Notes, tap the menu icon in the top left corner and select Backup. MYNOTESBACKUP files are created on the SD card of the Android device. To open a MYNOTESBACKUP file in Keep My Notes, tap the menu icon in the top left corner and select Restore. Android Keep My Notes.",
    "Android Keep My Notes.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".FLKB",
    "Folder Lock Basic Locker File",
    "2.5",
    "Encrypted archive, or locker, created by Folder Lock, an application used for protecting sensitive files; contains a collection of files that can only be opened using the locker password; uses NTFS file system formatting and supports unlimited file sizes; used for backing up personal documents and other sensitive files. FLKB files are referred to as Basic Lockers. Folder Lock also supports Portable Lockers (.FLKA extension), which have a 4GB file size limit. While Portable Lockers can be backed up using NewSoftwares online backup service, Basic Lockers cannot. NOTE: FLKB and FLKA files were introduced with version 7 of Folder Locker. Previous software versions use.FLK files for lockers. Windows NewSoftwares Folder Lock.",
    "Windows NewSoftwares Folder Lock.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".OEB",
    "Outlook Express Backup Wizard File",
    "2.5",
    "Electronic publication created in the legacy Open eBook (OEB) format, which was used by some publishers and eBook readers; contains the book index, chapters, and page content; superseded by the.EPUB format. The OEB standard was maintained by the Open eBook Forum, which is now the International Digital Publishing Forum (IDPF). Windows Geometer Plus FBReader. Mac Geometer Plus FBReader. Linux Geometer Plus FBReader. An OEB file is an Outlook Express e-mail database backup created by the Outlook Express Backup Wizard. It contains a complete backup of all Outlook Express files, including accounts, identities, e-mail messages, attachments, address books, message rules, lists of blocked senders, and signatures. Windows QSX Outlook Express Backup Wizard.",
    "Windows Geometer Plus FBReader. Mac Geometer Plus FBReader. Linux Geometer Plus FBReader. Windows QSX Outlook Express Backup Wizard.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".QV~",
    "ViewletBuilder Project Backup File",
    "2.5",
    "Backup file created by ViewletBuilder, an application used for building interactive Flash presentations; created when the.QVP project is saved and can be used for restoring the last saved state of the project by changing ~ to p and opening the file. Windows Qarbon ViewletBuilder. Mac Qarbon ViewletBuilder. Linux Qarbon ViewletBuilder.",
    "Windows Qarbon ViewletBuilder. Mac Qarbon ViewletBuilder. Linux Qarbon ViewletBuilder.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".CMF",
    "Connected Backup File",
    "2.5",
    "Three-dimensional mesh file created using Cal3D, a character animation library authored in C++; stores the 3D geometry of a character using polygons made up of nodes and edges; used for structuring the character. Cal3D meshes can also be stored in an XML form using the.XMF extension. Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3DFree. Audio file format developed by Creative Labs; designed to be used with Creative Sound Blaster sound cards and Creative software; can also be played by some third-party programs with supporting plug-ins installed. CMF files store music data as a series of notes, similar to a standard MIDI (.MID) file. However, they also contain instruments, which are used for playing back different sounds. NOTE: Sound Blaster Instrument (.SBI) files are similar to CMF files, but only contain instrument data. Windows Nullsoft Winamp with AdPlug pluginFree. Backup file created by Connected Backup, a program used for creating secure local and remote backups of computer data; stores backed up files in a secure proprietary format; can significantly reduce the size of the backup data, but may still be very large in size. CMF files can be used for backing up email data from Microsoft Outlook and IBM Lotus Notes. The softwares EmailOptimizer (EMO) component stores the backup CMF files in the following locations in Windows: [user]/​Email Backup Optimization/​Data C:/​ProgramData/​Email Backup Optimization/​Data/​Mail/​. Windows HP Connected Backup.",
    "Windows Cal3dViewer. Cal3d2ogre. Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Mac Short Fuze Limited Moviestorm. Linux Cal3D. Windows Nullsoft Winamp with AdPlug plugin. Windows HP Connected Backup.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".QBB",
    "QuickBooks Backup File",
    "2.5",
    "Backup file created by QuickBooks, a money management application; stores a full backup of company financial data, letters, templates, and logos; used for restoring the original data in the event that the primary.QBW is lost or becomes corrupted. QBB files are created by the Windows version of QuickBooks, but they may also be exported from the Mac version by choosing File → Back Up to QuickBooks for Windows.. from the application menu (QuickBooks 2012). NOTE: In some cases, you may need to change the file extension from .qbb to .qbw in order for the file to open correctly in QuickBooks. Windows Intuit QuickBooks Pro. Mac Intuit QuickBooks for Mac.",
    "Windows Intuit QuickBooks Pro. Mac Intuit QuickBooks for Mac.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".NWBAK",
    "NeatWorks Backup File",
    "2.4",
    "Backup file created by NeatWorks, which is an older version of the digital filing system software, Neat 5; similar to the.NBAK and.NRBAK files; contains a backup of your scanned documents, including contacts and receipts. To create a NWBAK file, select Tools → Database → Backup, use the default save name, click Browse, choose a save location, and click Backup. To restore a database in versions before Neat 5 using the NWBAK file, select Tools → Database → Restore, select Browse, navigate to your file, select Open, and then click Restore. In order to restore an old database such as the NWBAK file, you will need to run the Neat Data Migration Utility, select Browse, choose your backup file, provide a cabinet and database location, and click Migrate. NOTE: The NWBAK file extension replaced the NRBAK extension with the release of version 4.6 of NeatWorks. It was then used up until version 4.9 and was replaced by the NBAK extension with the release of Neat 5. Windows Neat.",
    "Windows Neat.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".WSPAK",
    "WebsitePanel Backup File",
    "2.4",
    "Backup file created by WebsitePanel, a portal application used for managing Windows Server applications such as IIS, SQL Server, Exchange, and Hyper-V; saves a backup of databases, settings, and other files on the server; can be used for migrating files to a new server; most often used by system administrators. WSPAK files are saved in a compressed.ZIP format, so you can view their contents manually with a Zip utility. However, they are typically not decompressed and extracted manually. NOTE: WebsitePanel only runs on Windows Server (i.e., not Windows Vista, 7, or 8). Windows WebsitePanel.",
    "Windows WebsitePanel.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".~CW",
    "Circuit Wizard Backup File",
    "2.4",
    "Temporary file created by Circuit Wizard, a circuit design and simulation program; saves a backup of a.CWZ circuit design file as its being edited in the software; allows the design to be restored in the event of a system crash or program failure. Windows New Wave Concepts Circuit Wizard.",
    "Windows New Wave Concepts Circuit Wizard.",
    "?"],
    ["backup_files",
    ".CBS",
    "Comodo Backup Script",
    "2.3",
    "Saved game state file created by Code Breaker, a PlayStation 2 (PS2) accessory program used to create game cheats and transfer saved games to a PC; contains saved state information for a specific game; used to load a preconfigured state in a PS2 games. CBS files can be converted to the.PSU and.MAX formats using the program mymc. Windows mymcFree. Backup script created by Comodo Backup, an application used for remote and local backups; may store instructions for a scheduled backup or a restore job; can be created from the Custom Backup view and run from with Comodo Backup. Windows Comodo BackupFree.",
    "Windows mymc. Windows Comodo Backup.",
    "?"],
